// Creo Explorer Property Handler — column mapping
//
// Place this file next to CreoExplorerHandler.dll (same folder).
// Edit mappings, then re-run Register.ps1 so Explorer column lists update.
// Explorer reads values from the DLL on each file open (no re-register needed
// just to change which Creo parameter feeds an already-registered column).
//
// Format (one mapping per line):
//   "Windows explorer detail header name" "CREO_PARAMETER_NAME"
//
// Lines that start with // are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
//
// Left side — either:
//   • An Explorer Details header alias (Authors, Tags, Company, …), or
//   • A Windows canonical name (System.Author, System.Company, …)
//
// Right side — exact Creo USER parameter name (Creo stores these UPPERCASE).
// Only String-type Creo parameters are shown; Real/Number values are skipped.
//
// Supported header aliases (also accept System.* forms):
//   Authors / Author          → System.Author
//   Tags / Keywords           → System.Keywords
//   Comments / Comment        → System.Comment
//   Title                     → System.Title
//   Subject                   → System.Subject
//   Company                   → System.Company
//   Category                  → System.Category
//   Status / Content status   → System.ContentStatus
//   Copyright                 → System.Copyright
//   Last author               → System.Document.LastAuthor
//   Revision / Revision number→ System.Document.RevisionNumber
//   Version / Version number  → System.Document.Version
//   Manager                   → System.Document.Manager
//   Client ID                 → System.Document.ClientID
//   Document ID               → System.Document.DocumentID
//   Contributor               → System.Document.Contributor
//   Language                  → System.Language
//   Source                    → System.Source
//   File description          → System.FileDescription
//   Software used             → System.SoftwareUsed
//   Application name          → System.ApplicationName
//   Content type              → System.ContentType
//
// Any other System.* string property name is also accepted on the left side.
// After adding a new System.* name, run Register.ps1 again, then enable the
// column in Explorer (right-click column header → More…).
//
// Default mappings (same as the built-in fallback if this file is missing):

"Authors" "AUTHORS"
"Tags" "TAGS"
"Comments" "COMMENTS"
"Title" "TITLE"
"Subject" "SUBJECT"

// Examples — uncomment and set your Creo parameter names:
// "Company" "COMPANY"
// "System.Document.RevisionNumber" "REV"
// "Category" "PRODUCT_LINE"
